#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:1
msgid "Decision to add a pi coding agent development environment to GitHub Codespaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:3
msgid "Status: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:4
msgid "Date: 2026-09-19"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:5
msgid "Decision-makers: tkoyama010"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:7
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:9
msgid "Contributors currently set up the development environment locally: the project uses [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for Python dependencies, npm for the TypeScript glue layer, and [pre-commit](https://pre-commit.com/) hooks (including the `pyadr` hooks that generate and check [`docs/decisions/`](./index.md)). [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) states that \"no local setup is required\" because CI verifies the environment on every PR, but a contributor or an AI coding agent still needs a working toolchain before the first commit. [pi](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-coding-agent) is the coding agent harness used to develop this repository, and [GitHub Codespaces](https://github.com/features/codespaces) can provision a ready-to-use browser or VS Code environment from a `devcontainer.json` file. Should we add a Codespaces development environment configured for the pi coding agent?"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:11
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:13
msgid "**Low-friction onboarding**: a contributor should be able to start hacking (or run the pi agent) with one click, without installing uv, Node, or pre-commit locally."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:14
msgid "**Agent parity**: the pi agent works best when the environment it edits in matches CI exactly, so agent-made PRs pass on the first run."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:15
msgid "**Single source of truth**: the environment definition must live in the repository and be versioned with the code, like every other tool decision here."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:16
msgid "**Maintenance cost**: pyvista-wasm is a small project; a second environment definition that drifts from the local/CI one is a real liability."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:17
msgid "**No local setup required**: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) promises CI verifies the environment; a Codespace must not become a requirement to contribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:19
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:21
msgid "**Option A: Add a Codespaces devcontainer configured for the pi coding agent**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:22
msgid "**Option B: Keep local setup only (status quo)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:24
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:26
msgid "Chosen option: \"**Option A: Add a Codespaces devcontainer configured for the pi coding agent**\", because it is the only option that makes the environment reproducible for both human contributors and the pi agent at zero marginal CI cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:28
msgid "The devcontainer installs the same toolchain CI uses: Python via uv, Node.js via npm, and pre-commit with all hooks from [`.pre-commit-config.yaml`](../../.pre-commit-config.yaml)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:29
msgid "The pi CLI is installed in the image, so an agent session starts with the repository, [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md), and the lint/test commands already available."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:30
msgid "The environment definition is one `devcontainer.json` (plus a small Dockerfile if needed) under `.devcontainer/`, versioned in the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:31
msgid "CI remains the source of truth for \"does the environment work\": the Codespace reuses the same install steps, so drift is visible in PRs."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:33
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:35
msgid "Good, because contributors and the pi agent get a working, CI-equivalent environment in minutes with no local installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:36
msgid "Good, because agent-driven changes (the primary development workflow for this repository) start from the same tool versions CI enforces."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:37
msgid "Good, because the Codespace definition documents the environment as code; setup steps stop living in people's heads."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:38
msgid "Bad, because a second environment surface can drift from CI; any toolchain change must update CI and the devcontainer together."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:39
msgid "Bad, because Codespaces consumption is billed per core-hour; occasional contributors may prefer local setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:41
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:43
msgid "Compliance is confirmed by the presence of `.devcontainer/` in the repository and by launching a Codespace from a PR preview: `uv run pytest`, `npm run lint`, and `pre-commit run --all-files` must succeed inside it without manual installation steps. If `.devcontainer/` is removed, or if it no longer reproduces the CI toolchain, this decision is violated."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:45
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:47
msgid "Option A: Add a Codespaces devcontainer configured for the pi coding agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:49
msgid "A `devcontainer.json` under `.devcontainer/` that installs uv, Node.js, pre-commit, and the pi CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:51
msgid "Good, because onboarding becomes one click for humans and one `gh codespace create` for agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:52
msgid "Good, because the pi agent can be pointed at a fresh Codespace per task, keeping sessions isolated and reproducible."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:53
msgid "Good, because the definition is versioned and reviewed like code."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:54
msgid "Neutral, because the devcontainer reuses the same commands CI already runs; it adds no new tool to maintain."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:55
msgid "Bad, because Codespaces usage costs money and requires a GitHub account with the feature enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:56
msgid "Bad, because image build time must be kept in check or Codespace startup becomes slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:58
msgid "Option B: Keep local setup only (status quo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:60
msgid "Contributors and agents run against local machines; CI verifies the result on every PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:62
msgid "Good, because no new files or image builds are maintained."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:63
msgid "Good, because [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) already promises CI covers environment verification."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:64
msgid "Bad, because every contributor and every fresh agent session repeats setup manually, with version drift between machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:65
msgid "Bad, because the pi agent cannot reliably start from a clean, known-good state; agent PR quality depends on the host machine it happens to run on."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:67
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:69
msgid "Toolchain sources of truth: [`pyproject.toml`](../../pyproject.toml) / `uv.lock`, [`package.json`](../../package.json) / `package-lock.json`, [`.pre-commit-config.yaml`](../../.pre-commit-config.yaml)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:70
msgid "Environment promises in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) must be kept in sync if this decision is revisited."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:71
msgid "Revisit triggers: Codespace costs become a problem, or the devcontainer drifts from CI and the drift cannot be closed cheaply."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0013-decision-to-add-a-pi-coding-agent-development-environment-to-github-codespaces.md:72
msgid "Follow-up decision: [ADR-0014 — Decision not to use Nix in the Codespace environment](0014-decision-not-to-use-nix-in-the-codespace-environment.md)."
msgstr ""
